- op: discuss  # ff69
  at: '2026-05-12T09:55:50Z'  # ff69
  by: agent  # ff69
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ff69
  clock: 3  # ff69
  nonce: ff69  # ff69
  message: "Fixed in PR #3660. The dominant cause of django's empty rslice.1.prod.json was a structural bug in is_utility_file: the 'ambiguous dirs at any depth unless we've already passed a source root' rule false-positived on packages whose top-level directory isn't in the hardcoded _SOURCE_ROOTS set ({src, lib, app, crates, packages}). Django, requests, urllib3, flask, and similar pip-shipped packages use the package name itself as the top-level directory, so every nested utils/, contrib/, etc. was flagged. Fix: ambiguous dirs (now including contrib and hack) only match at path_parts[0] == 0 (the repo root). +1 regression test covering Django/requests/urllib3/flask + root-level guards. Chatwoot/nestjs sub-symptoms investigated and not currently reproducible — see PR body and CHANGELOG note."  # ff69
